ellys so  he and his team are sending out seed for  testing and further improvements in  other countries  but much more breeding and testing needs  to be done and dealing with this latest  form of virulent we trust won't be the  end of humanity's long battle with the  fungus Borlaug warned the scientists at  the meeting that the international  network of monitoring for wheat rest  needs to be strengthened and maintained  stem rust never sleeps it keeps changing  every day and night is unpredictable  often people only react to crises like  crop failures but given the importance  of wheat for feeding the world many  scientists hope that Borlaug's warning  will have a lasting effect this is Eric  stock stead with science magazine  you
 

